meta {
  name: AnalysisRuns
  seq: 4
}

docs {
  `AnalysisRunController` — the unified analysis engine. One Claude call runs per selected source
  document (IEP, ETR, or progress report) and a synthesis call runs once 2+ sources complete, so a
  single `AnalysisRun` can span multiple documents for a child and carry a cross-document summary.

  Replaces the legacy per-document endpoints (`POST/GET /api/ieps/{id}/analyze|analysis`,
  `POST/GET /api/etrs/{id}/analyze|analysis`), which are removed — there were no Bruno requests for
  them to retire.

  Access: Viewer+ can list/read runs; Collaborator+ is required to create one. Every created run
  reserves one unit of the child's analysis quota (5 per child) regardless of outcome — a run whose
  sources all fail is refunded unless any failure was an unparseable model response (then the unit is
  kept, since a document engineered to always produce unparseable JSON must not be a free retry loop);
  a partially successful run is not refunded.

  `AnalysisRunController.MapFailure` maps a failed service call to a status code by sniffing the
  message text, not a typed error: a message containing "subscription" → `402`, "permission" → `403`,
  anything else (including "Child not found.") → `400`. `GetById` and `GetLatestForSource` don't use
  `MapFailure` — every failure on those two (not found, no access, or no matching run) is `404`.
}
